 real network round-trip PER TOKEN. Splitting a model across N machines doesn't parallelize compute like data-parallel batching does; it adds N-1 network hops to every token's critical path.\", :operational-corollary \"RPC-distributing is a CAPACITY mechanism (use when a model's weights don't fit in the head's ~46GB alone), NOT a speed mechanism. qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b (22GB) never needed it — serve-standalone was correct the whole time. Still valuable for genuinely oversized models (e.g. the retired glm-5.2-reap50-q2k, 139GB, doesn't fit any single node here) where 17 tok/s distributed beats 0 tok/s (doesn't run at all).\", :fleet-state-after \"reverted to standalone-on-head; both RPC numbers registered in /infer/models and GET /itonami/perf alongside the standalone number\"}", :adr/follow-ups-not-done ["fix cmd-down/cmd-ps pgrep pattern mismatch" "wire serve-standalone into plan/provision orchestration instead of a parallel manual-ish path" "/v1/messages/count_tokens unimplemented"], :adr/date "2026-07-04..2026-07-05", :adr/decisions "{:1-base-models {:retired [\"glm-5.2-reap50-q2k\" \"qwen3-next-80b-a3b\" \"gemma-4-26b-a4b\"], :added [{:id \"qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b\", :size-gib 20.6} {:id \"qwen3.6-35b-a3b\", :size-gib 19.7} {:id \"gemma-4-12b-it\", :size-gib 6.6}], :verified-via \"bb murakumo infer plan (all FIT against live fleet, 110.9 GiB total usable)\", :incidental-fixes [\"stale itonami-verticals model refs (2512/2432/2356)\" \"infer_view.cljc kotoba.html require -> real html.core/->html namespace\"]}, :2-live-deploy {:model \"qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b\", :fleet \"6x Apple M4 mini (rpc-server, Metal) + 1 AMD head 'gad' (llama-server)\", :verified \"real /v1/chat/completions completion, not just health check\", :cloudflare-tailscale-gap {:problem \"Cloudflare edge cannot reach head's Tailscale CGNAT IP directly\", :fix \"hostname route infer.murakumo.cloud -> localhost:8090 added to head's existing cloudflared tunnel (id c75a3e83-6cef-4d9b-ba22-fbb459ee6fbe,