clj-datomic/compare\", :qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b {:passed 6, :total 6, :avg-tok-s 12.67, :budget \"2500 (4500 for 2/6)\"}, :gemma-4-12b-it {:passed 1, :total 6, :avg-tok-s 7.54, :budget \"4000 (3/6 non-convergent; fib-memo re-verified passing @ 8000 tokens)\", :genuine-failures [\"wrong Datomic keyword namespacing (:db/string vs :db.type/string)\" \"invalid Clojure syntax: extra parens around map literal -> 0-arg fn call\"]}, :verdict \"qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b wins clearly; dense 12B loses to 35B-total/3B-active MoE despite being smaller\", :fleet-state-after \"switched back to qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b\"}, :6-standalone-gpu {:finding \"head ('gad', AMD Ryzen AI MAX+ 395 Strix Halo, Radeon 8060S iGPU) ran a CPU-only llama-server build — no Vulkan/ROCm linked, -ngl 999 was a no-op\", :mac-minis-checked \"confirmed GPU-accelerated the whole time: ggml_metal_init: found device: Apple M4\", :fix {:binary \"official llama.cpp Vulkan release (llama-b9873-bin-ubuntu-vulkan-x64.tar.gz) — Mesa/RADV detects Radeon 8060S Graphics (RADV GFX1151)\", :topology \"standalone on head only, no RPC ring (model fits in head's ~46GB RAM)\", :new-command \"bb murakumo infer serve-standalone <model> [gguf] (cmd-serve-standalone)\", :config-key \":infer/head :standalone-bin-dir\"}, :result {:before-tok-s 12.67, :after-tok-s 61.5, :speedup \"~4.8x\"}, :rocm-attempt {:build \"llama-b9873-bin-ubuntu-rocm-7.2-x64.tar.gz\", :result \"detects no device — gfx1151/Strix Halo not yet ROCm-supported\", :workarounds-tried [\"HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.0.0\"], :outcome \"abandoned, Vulkan is the working path\"}, :known-unfixed-bug \"bb murakumo infer down / cmd-ps pgrep pattern ('.murakumo/bin/rpc-server') doesn't match actual argv0 (./rpc-server, relative) — down has never actually killed a worker; harmless while serve-standalone doesn't need the ring\"}}", :adr/addendum-2026-07-05-part8-model-map "{:landing-incident \"a `git diff ... > file.patch` redirect silently produced an EMPTY file (shell cwd had reset between tool calls without notice), and the immediately-following `git checkout --` reverted the shared checkout's working tree before the patch was verified non-empty — local-murakumo's changes were briefly lost from disk. Recovered by re-applying the exact edits from this conversation's own tool-call history onto a fresh worktree (no data was actually unrecoverable — the edits existed as this session's own record). Lesson: wc -l the patch file before running any revert that depends on it.\", :built {:cmd \"bb murakumo infer media model-map [--push] (kotoba-lang/murakumo, new cmd-model-map in media.clj) — queries head's own /v1/models for the live text model (matched to infer.edn by GGUF filename), reuses live-fleet's ComfyUI checkpoint probe for media nodes, matches each checkpoint 3 ways: :exact / :family-guess (small hand-maintained alias table) / :unregistered\", :routes \"GET/POST /infer/model-map + GET /infer/model-map/ui (gftdcojp/local-murakumo) — a THIRD distinct KV doc, separate from hwmetrics (hardware only) and /infer/placement (rebalancer's desired allocation, not what's actually resident — naming collision avoided deliberately)\", :ui \"merges model-map + latest hwmetrics snapshot into one node x category table; nodes with no media model loaded still show up as 'no media model loaded', not omitted\"}, :research-finding \"murakumo-studio (ADR-2607032700) is the WRONG place — single-machine LM-Studio-equivalent desktop app, fleet participation is announce-only, no multi-node dashboard. Real building blocks existed but were scattered/hidden: bb murakumo infer media nodes already queried per-node ComfyUI checkpoints (real data) but CLI-only, never exposed as a UI; /infer/hwmetrics has per-node hardware but zero model identity; text-to-3D is a genuine content gap (no model registered anywhere), not a query gap.\", :real-drift-surfaced \"naphtali/issachar actually run ltxv-2b-0.9.6-distilled-04-25.safetensors, not the ltx-video-2b-v0.9.1.safetensors registered in infer.edn for ltxv-2b-0.9.1 — labelled :family-guess with an explicit 'drifted from infer.edn' note, not hidden\", :known-simplification \"text placement reports only the single serving node (the head, standalone-GPU architecture) — an RPC-ring deployment would need .murakumo-infer-plan.edn's shard assignments for real per-node breakdown, not implemented\", :cadence \"model-map is pushed ON-DEMAND by an operator, not a continuous ~10s feed like hwmetrics — /ui is plain SSR, no live poller, by design\", :text-to-3d-handling \"explicit 'unsupported' card with the honest reason (no registered model) — same norm as gguf/mlx/kotoba honesty in catalog.cljc part 6\", :verified-live [\"api.murakumo.cloud/infer/model-map\" \"api.murakumo.cloud/infer/model-map/ui\" \"/infer/hwmetrics unaffected (separate KV doc, no regression)\"], :trigger \"user: is there a UI showing which terminal has which model loaded, across text/image/video/audio/text-to-3D?\"}", :adr/addendum-2026-07-05-part5-parallel-2-reverted-to-1 "{:trigger \"same day, parallel=2 live in production: 2 real Claude Code sessions ended up active simultaneously\", :observed {:slot-a \"session doing repeated tool-call round-trips, reprocessing 14K-28K-token growing prompts per turn, some cancelled+relaunched (LCP similarity sim_best=0.460 — under half the prompt prefix-cache-hit)\", :slot-b \"a DIFFERENT session's generation crawled to 0.24-0.38 tok/s (tg_3s), ~250x slower than the ~60 tok/s baseline, for as long as slot-a's heavy prefill ran\"}, :root-cause \"2 logical slots share ONE physical GPU. llama-server does not time-slice fairly between a slot doing heavy prompt processing (compute-heavy, can dominate the device for tens of seconds) and another slot trying to decode (needs frequent small time-slices) — the prefill-heavy slot starves the decode-only slot.\", :verdict \"parallel=2's real-world failure mode under genuine concurrent load is BOTH sessions degrade together — worse for a human waiting on either one than parallel=1's failure mode (one request queues completely but gets the FULL ~60 tok/s the instant its turn comes: a bounded, predictable wait vs. an unbounded crawl for both parties)\", :action \"reverted serve-standalone default parallel: 2 -> 1, same day\", :not-fixed \"the actual root cause from part4 (llama-server not promptly detecting a dead/killed client connection) is STILL unfixed — would need a server-side request/idle timeout, not attempted. This revert just accepts 'a second request queues and waits' as the more predictable failure mode for this hardware's real usage pattern (rarely more than one active claude-murakumo session at a time).\", :verified [\"restarted with parallel=1, confirmed n_slots=1 in server log\" \"confirmed a real in-flight request completed at the expected 60.05 tok/s baseline once it had the slot to itself\"]}", :db/id -1, :adr/addendum-2026-07-05-speed-parallelism-context "{:trigger \"real Claude Code request measured 65561 tokens, 25 over the then-current 65536 ctx -> exceed_context_size_error\", :single-stream-perspective {:this-fleet-tok-s 61.5, :hosted-comparison [{:model \"Claude Sonnet 5 (Max Effort)\", :tok-s 72.0, :source \"artificialanalysis.ai 2026-07\"}], :verdict \"a consumer APU with no discrete GPU lands in the same tok/s range as a hosted flagship model served from a datacenter GPU cluster — 300 tok/s was never a realistic single-stream target for ANY mainstream hosted model, let alone this hardware\", :bottleneck \"memory bandwidth: decode reads ~3B active MoE params (Q4_K_M) from LPDDR5x once per token\"}, :parallelism-measured {:method \"N concurrent /v1/chat/completions requests, wall-clock aggregate = sum(completion_tokens)/wall_seconds\", :results [{:n 1, :aggregate-tok-s 53.8} {:n 2, :aggregate-tok-s 77.1} {:n 4, :aggregate-tok-s 107.8} {:n 6, :aggregate-tok-s 121.2, :note \"peak\"} {:n 8, :aggregate-tok-s 74.6, :note \"regressed\"}], :caveat \"raises AGGREGATE throughput only via continuous batching; a single Claude Code conversation (one request in flight) still sees ~61.5 tok/s regardless of --parallel\"}, :context-ceiling {:landed 262144, :reason \"qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b's own GGUF-declared native training context (qwen35moe.context_length) — confirmed by direct testing to be the real hard ceiling on the current llama-server binary\", :architecture \"hybrid Gated-DeltaNet(SSM)/Gated-Attention, full_attention_interval=4 — only 10/40 layers need real KV cache (5GB f16 at 262144); the other 30 use a FIXED ~63MB recurrent state independent of context length\", :1m-yarn-attempt {:flags-tried \"--rope-scaling yarn --yarn-orig-ctx 262144 --rope-scale 4 -c 1010000\", :result \"llama-server capped back to 262144 regardless\", :root-cause \"known upstream bug: server hard-caps -c to n_ctx_train unconditionally, ignoring explicit YaRN override flags\", :github-issues [\"ggml-org/llama.cpp#22140 (closed, not planned)\" \"ggml-org/llama.cpp#17459 (open, unconfirmed)\"], :real-fix \"patch tools/server source + rebuild from source — no CLI-flag workaround exists on official release binaries\", :hypothetical-memory-at-1m {:kv-f16-gib 19.26, :kv-q8_0-gib 9.63, :model-gib 20.6, :verdict \"f16 combined ~40GB (tight vs ~46GB unified RAM); q8_0 combined ~30GB (comfortable) — confirmed q8_0/q8_0 --cache-type-k/v loads+serves correctly on this Vulkan backend at unchanged speed, so this is real future headroom IF the server cap is ever lifted\"}, :status \"not attempted (source rebuild); logged as follow-up\"}}, :landed-changes [\":infer/ctx 262144\" \":infer/flash-attn \\\"on\\\" (measured no speed difference vs auto, set explicitly anyway)\" \"cmd-serve-standalone accepts optional parallel arg\" \"fixed kill-then-relaunch race: fixed 0.5s sleep after kill -9 wasn't always enough for the port to free before rebind; now polls pgrep until process is gone\"], :exposed-at \"GET /itonami/perf (api.murakumo.cloud)\"}", :adr/problem "{:found \"GET /infer/models and GET /nodes